  <div class="outer-wrapper page-title">
    
<h1  class="h1 h1--with-wrapper h1--page-title">
  
  
    <span>High-Reliability and Low-Latency Communications for 6G Network: ISAC-Enabled Architectures, Networking, and Services </span>

  </h1>
  </div>


  
  
    
      <article  class="node node--type-call-for-papers  node--view-mode-full">

  
    

      <div class="outer-wrapper outer-wrapper-menu">
      <div class="cpf-type">Special Issue</div>
    </div>
  
  
  <div class="outer-wrapper outer-wrapper-menu">

            
  
  <div id="p-77861" class="paragraph-anchor-wrapper">
  <a href="#p-77861" class="paragraph-anchor-link " aria-label="Copy link to this section" title="Copy link to this section">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg>
</a>
<div>
  

            <div class="text-long"><h2>Important Dates</h2><p><strong>Manuscript Submission Deadline:</strong> 15 September 2026 (Extended Deadline)<br><strong>Initial Decision:</strong> 1 December 2026<br><strong>Revision Manuscript Due:</strong> 1 January 2027<br><strong>Final Decision:</strong> 1 February 2027<br><strong>Final Manuscript Due:</strong> 15 February 2027<br><strong>Publication Date:</strong> May 2027</p><h2>Scope</h2><p>The rise of mission-critical 6G applications, such as autonomous systems, intelligent transportation, industrial automation, emergency response, and large-scale sensing, imposes stringent requirements on ultra-high reliability, ultra-low latency, and real-time situational awareness, exceeding the capabilities of existing terrestrial networks. In line with the IMT-2030 vision, 6G calls for tight latency guarantees, extreme reliability, and deep integration of communication, sensing, computation, and control. Integrated sensing and communication (ISAC) have thus emerged as a key enabler, empowering networks with joint connectivity and environmental awareness.&nbsp;</p><p>This Special Issue (SI) focuses on high-reliability and low-latency 6G networking from an ISAC perspective, emphasizing network-centric architectures, protocols, and services. Contributions addressing theory, system design, standardization, and experimental validation are welcome to advance scalable and intelligent 6G systems.</p><p>Topics of interest include, but are not limited to:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>6G network architectures for high-reliability and low-latency services.</li><li>Integrated heterogeneous communication and networking.&nbsp;</li><li>ISAC-enabled network architectures, protocols, and services.&nbsp;</li><li>Advanced waveform design for ISAC systems.&nbsp;</li><li>Coding, modulation, and HARQ mechanisms for URLLC.&nbsp;</li><li>Passive, semi-passive, and network-based sensing and localization.&nbsp;</li><li>Deterministic and time-sensitive networking for mission-critical 6G services.&nbsp;</li><li>AI-native communication and sensing for reliability and latency optimization.&nbsp;</li><li>Joint communication-sensing-computation networking architectures.&nbsp;</li><li>Mobility management and ultra-fast handover for aerial platforms.&nbsp;</li><li>Security, safety, and resilience in ISAC-enabled 6G networks.&nbsp;</li><li>Standardization, regulation, and spectrum challenges for 6G networking.&nbsp;</li><li>Experimental testbeds, prototyping platforms, field trials, and system validation.&nbsp;</li></ul><h2>Submission Guidelines</h2><p>Manuscripts should conform to the standard format as indicated in the “Information for Authors” section of the&nbsp;<a href="/publications/magazines/ieee-network/policies-guidelines">Policies and Guidelines</a>.</p><p>All manuscripts to be considered for publication must be submitted by the deadline through the magazine’s&nbsp;<a href="https://ieee.atyponrex.com/journal/network-ieee" target="_blank">IEEE Author Portal</a>&nbsp;submission site. Select the appropriate issue date and topic from the “Please Select an Article Type” drop-down menu.</p><h2>Guest Editors</h2><p><a href="mailto:markku.juntti@oulu.fi"><strong>Markku Juntti </strong></a><strong>(Co-Lead Guest Editor)</strong>, University of Oulu, Finland&nbsp;<br><a href="mailto:fangyi@gdut.edu.cn"><strong>Yi Fang</strong></a><strong> (Co-Lead Guest Editor)</strong>, Guangdong University of Technology, China&nbsp;<br><a href="mailto: jiguang.he@gbu.edu.cn"><strong>Jiguang He</strong></a>, Great Bay University, China&nbsp;<br><a href="mailto:yonghui.li@sydney.edu.au"><strong>Yonghui Li</strong></a>, The University of Sydney, Australia<br><a href="mailto:merouane.debbah@ku.ac.ae"><strong>Merouane Debbah</strong></a>, Khalifa University of Science and Technology, UAE&nbsp;<br><a href="mailto:xianbin.wang@uwo.ca"><strong>Xianbin Wang</strong></a>, Western University, Canada<br><a href="mailto:iqbal.hussain@ericsson.com"><strong>Iqbal Hussain</strong></a><strong>,&nbsp;</strong>Ericsson, Sweden&nbsp;</p></div>
      
</div>

  </div>

